ar":1993,"pageCount":528,"summary":"This is a fascinating and disturbing tale that illustrates just how hard it is to convict somebody who has a lot of money and power. Cullen Davis, warped little rich boy dominated by his incredibly wealthy and megalomanic father, grows up to inherit most of the fortune and position. What does he do with it? He chases sex kitten type women, showers them with lavish gifts, and abuses them. Naifeh and Smith raise the true crime genre to something close to literature here. We have the usual litany of sickies and psychopaths, the usual police incompetence, prosecutors who can't prosecute, etc. The \"final justice\" in the title is somewhat ironic since multimillionaire Cullen Davis is never found guilty of any of his crimes, the worst of which was the cold-blooded murder of his wife's 12-year-old daughter; the least of which, perhaps the killing of her kitten.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7945672-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0.138,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"popular","score":0.22,"confidence":"low","evidence":["trade publisher signal: Dutton / Penguin Random House"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":false,"publicFame":3,"criticalRenown":5,"controversy":0,"llmAffinity":52,"affinityResidual":-16.03,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.1,"criticalRenown":0.1,"controversy":0.1,"llmAffinity":0.2},"tags":{"craft":"narrative-drive","evidence":"none","stance":"none"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"displaySummary":"This is a fascinating and disturbing tale that illustrates just how hard it is to convict somebody who has a lot of money and power. Cullen Davis, warped little rich boy dominated by his incredibly wealthy and megalomanic father, grows up to inherit most of the fortune and position. What does he do with it? He chases sex kitten type women, showers them with lavish gifts, and abuses them. Naifeh